## What problem are you trying to solve?
The current functions required to write a rule can be hard to remember, even with IDE type hints ("is it buildError? newError?"). It's hard especially because everything is exposed as a JavaScript global, so there are no hints as to which functions exist.
```js
                        if (node.astType === "return_statement") {
                            if(node.children.length === 1 && node.children[0].astType === "null_literal") {
/* global function -> */        addError(
/* global function -> */            buildError(
                                        node.start.line, node.start.col,
                                        node.end.line, node.end.col,
                                        "ToString() should never return null"
                                    )
                                );
                            }
                        }
```

## What is your solution?

We will be redesigning the JavaScript API to be based around a single entrypoint: `ddsa`.

This PR does not implement a complete revamp of the API: it serves as an initial structure for the `ddsa` entrypoint so contributors can use it as a template for converting other functions.

Thus, this PR implements the `getChildren(...)` function. Example usage:

```js
const ids = ddsa.getChildren(node).filter((n) => n.type === "identifier");
```

